 "findings": [
  {
   "id": "F1",
   "severity": "amendment",
   "check": "5 fairness",
   "finding": "Every rho arm (rho, rho2, rho2x, rhoseq) starts each target walk at Q plus two bank points (two counted affine additions) and repeats this at every 32-step restart in phase 2. IC4 and bsgs2 pay no per-target start because their trial progressions are shared. An anchored walk can start at Q itself, so this is avoidable overhead in the reference. An instrumented scratch build left the counters unchanged on all 2112 rows. It measured 1.07 to 2.07 starts per target at kappa 0.7: 2.1 to 4.1 GAE/target, or 2.5% to 3.2% of each rho run's total at I = 10M, h = 0. In a validator counterfactual that removes this cost from every rho run, IC4 is still cheaper at T = 16384 for every I/M and h: medians 0.932 to 0.978, largest 95% upper bound 0.982. T = 4096 becomes dearer at I = 10M and 30M and stays unranked at 3M; T = 1024 stays dearer. The headline holds against this overhead. The measured 5% to 9% margin narrows to 2% to 7%, and the T = 4096 'unranked' depends on it.",
   "unquantified": "Phase-1 walk waste: rho2/rho2x store 1.64 to 1.87 x-classes per step, against an ideal of 2, and phase-1 restarts cost 1.2% to 2.5% of total. Sibling self-duplicates: when the step's arm equals the previous step's arm, x(prev - A) is the previous walk point. By the arm-draw probability this is about 4.6% of steps; it was estimated, not measured.",
   "evidence": "VALIDATOR_REPORT.md section 5; validator scratch out/sens.json, out/replay_dbg.jsonl"
  },
  {
   "id": "F2",
   "severity": "amendment",
   "check": "5 fairness / reporting",
   "finding": "Every arm includes the counted double-and-add verification of every recovered log in I/M/S. It is identical across the 16 runs of every configuration (132/132) and costs 31.6 to 36.3 GAE/target at I = 10M. For IC4 at 24 b, T = 16384 that is 34.7 of 63.8 GAE/target. No attack pays this cost, and adding it to both arms pulls every ratio toward 1. RESULTS.md does not disclose it, although the v1 validator's amendment 4 asked for it. With verification removed from every arm, IC4/rhobest is 0.840 to 0.929 at T = 16384, 0.941 to 1.045 at T = 4096 and 1.078 to 1.209 at T = 1024; IC4/bsgs2 is 1.49 to 2.04. All section-5a verdicts are unchanged.",
   "evidence": "VALIDATOR_REPORT.md sections 5 and 6"
  },
  {
   "id": "F3",
   "severity": "amendment",
   "check": "reporting contract",
   "finding": "RESULTS.md does not separate phases. They exist only in rows.jsonl, and v1 amendment 5 asked for them. The validator's phase table is in VALIDATOR_REPORT.md section 6.",
   "evidence": "VALIDATOR_REPORT.md section 6"
  },
  {
   "id": "F4",
   "severity": "amendment",
   "check": "6 recompute / wording",
   "finding": "'Strongest rho' means the cheapest of the four pre-registered rho arms in this harness. It is not the strongest possible rho (F1), so the wording should say that. rho2x is the minimum in 51 of the 54 (cell, I/M, h) settings, in all 22 configurations of each. rho2 is the minimum in the other 3 (24 b, T = 16384, I = 30M). rho and rhoseq are never the minimum. The RESULTS spot check ('17 of the 18') agrees with this but should cite the full count. bsgs2 is a generic method in the same harness with the same shared-inversion lever, and IC4 is dearer than it everywhere (1.18x to 1.80x as measured). That disclosure must stay next to the rho ratio.",
   "evidence": "validator scratch out/recompute.json (rhobest_winner_by_setting)"
  },
  {
   "id": "F5",
   "severity": "amendment",
   "check": "6 recompute / wording",
   "finding": "RESULTS says that at T = 4096 IC4 is 'cheaper at h = 0 and 0.1, dearer at h = 1'. That is inexact at 25 b. At I = 30M the h = 0.1 median is 1.005 [1.001, 1.011] and the h = 0 interval includes 1 [0.993, 1.003]; at I = 10M the h = 0.1 interval is [0.992, 1.002]. The 'unranked' verdict is correct.",
   "evidence": "validator scratch out/recompute.json"
  },
  {
   "id": "F6",
   "severity": "process",
   "check": "artifact policy (AGENTS.md section 13)",
   "finding": "rows.jsonl (1,446,974 bytes, .jsonl) is committed to Git at the validated commit, against the artifact-store policy for data-suffixed files over 64 KiB. The bench record's raw entry says uploaded: false, with status open and validation null. The phase snapshots and argv that this validation replayed exist only in rows.jsonl. It must be uploaded and hash-verified (sha256 cafb8c71...4997a7a) before it leaves Git. runs.json carries totals only.",
   "evidence": "benchmarks/records/20261111T0142Z-mt-fieldops-ic4-v2.json"
  },
  {
   "id": "F7",
   "severity": "note",
   "check": "reproducibility bindings",
   "finding": "Each row binds the commit (6b0ac6f192) and the binary SHA (bbcc68cc...). The rows have no dirty-tree flag and no toolchain. The bench record has commit_dirty false at init (01:42:08Z) and isolation 'unstated'. The run was on a local host, not isolab-eks; Limits discloses this. Counts are deterministic: a scratch build of the frozen source (rustc 1.97.0, rand 0.8.8, serde_json 1.0.151) reproduces all 2112 rows exactly. No wall-clock figure is used.",
   "evidence": "VALIDATOR_REPORT.md section 3"
  },
  {
   "id": "F8",
   "severity": "process",
   "check": "AGENTS.md section 12 (ecbench)",
   "finding": "This is not an ecbench session: there is no ecbench.spec and no 'ecbench verify --replay' receipt. This certificate is an independent replay of the producer-written harness, not an ecbench receipt. RESULTS should name the section-12 deviation explicitly.",
   "evidence": "study directory listing"
  },
  {
   "id": "F9",
   "severity": "note",
   "check": "scope",
   "finding": "The working tree moved during validation. HEAD advanced to 2ad87dd980 (01:49:53Z), which adds an IC-leaderboard section labelled 'not validated' plus benchmark figures. That commit is outside the validated artifact set: dbbc139ef5, read from a git-archive copy. Its table reads summary.json at I = 10M, which this validation reproduces exactly. Its builder change and rendered pages were not validated.",
   "evidence": "git log; VALIDATOR_REPORT.md section 0"
  },
  {
   "id": "F10",
   "severity": "amendment",
   "check": "reporting (AGENTS.md section 3)",
   "finding": "'Where IC4 wins and why' is an explanation the experiment does not test, so it should be labelled as interpretation. RESULTS gives no section-3 class. The v1-to-v2 IC4 code change is an accounting correction: it adds a counted hash, which raises IC4's cost. The row is a cross-method comparison, not an improvement over an IC baseline.",
   "evidence": "RESULTS.md; git diff 3434954e47 6b0ac6f192 -- examples/mt_fieldops.rs"
  },
  {
   "id": "F11",
   "severity": "note",
   "check": "2 instances",
   "finding": "The 33 instances are valid (p and n prime, by Miller-Rabin and by trial division; nonsingular; G on the curve; [n]G = O; n in the Hasse interval, so #E = n; fixture point = [known_log]G). They regenerate byte-identically from the declared command (gen_instances.py, blob 5a04d358, unchanged since 2026-11-06; seed mtfo-v2-20261111). The scan covered 119,742 JSON/JSONL files under research/ (30,652 distinct (p, a, b) curve records) and 20,886 records in docs/curves: no exact match, no isomorphic match (same p, j and n) and no same-j curve. One earlier curve has the same (p, n) and a different j, so it is isogenous, not the same curve: W22-9 vs research/ic_e222_m221_20261106/results/instances_scale/W22-6.json. W22-5 and W22-10 share (p, n) within the set, with different j. No instance has a = 0 or b = 0, so negation is the only automorphism and the x-only lookups are the strongest symmetry available to the rho arms.",
   "evidence": "VALIDATOR_REPORT.md section 2"
  },
  {
   "id": "F12",
   "severity": "note",
   "check": "5 fairness",
   "finding": "No uncounted field or hash work was found in rho2x, rhoseq or the ic4 change. rho2x costs I + 3M + 2S per step, with the correct x-only sibling formula. A hit on a stored x-only sibling recomputes it with a counted padd, and the target-side sibling's y is recomputed with a counted padd. rhoseq's phase 1 costs one counted padd and one counted hash per entry; its phase 2 is identical to rho. The ic4 dedupe lookup is now counted, one f.hash per table hit in phase 1. The v1-to-v2 diff of mt_fieldops.rs is exactly these hunks plus comments, so rho, rho2 and bsgs2 are byte-identical to v1. Every arm leaves F_p additions, subtractions and negations and mod-n log arithmetic uncounted. The source header discloses this; RESULTS does not. Pricing the mod-n work would cost the rho arms more than IC4.",
   "evidence": "examples/mt_fieldops.rs at 6b0ac6f192"
  },
  {
   "id": "F13",
   "severity": "note",
   "check": "m=83 / ECC2K-130",
   "finding": "Not engaged: these are prime-field toy curves and no ECC2K-130 transfer is claimed. The row text should say so in one line.",
